---
title: What one unattended daily sweep actually does
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant EB as EventBridge
    participant AG as radar-agent
    participant CAT as Bedrock<br/>control plane
    participant TGT as Live targets<br/>(Bedrock/Comprehend/Translate)
    participant DB as DynamoDB
    participant SNS as SNS

    EB->>AG: {"mode":"sweep"} · 09:00 UTC

    rect rgba(184, 241, 74, 0.18)
    note over AG,TGT: Phase 1 — reachability
    AG->>CAT: ListFoundationModels + ListInferenceProfiles<br/>× 4 regions
    CAT-->>AG: full text-model catalog
    AG->>TGT: one-token probe per watched dependency
    TGT-->>AG: answered / refused / errored
    note right of AG: the probe is the authority.<br/>the catalog lists models<br/>you may not be entitled to call.
    end

    rect rgba(125, 200, 255, 0.18)
    note over AG,SNS: Phase 2 — diff against yesterday
    AG->>DB: read previous SNAPSHOT
    DB-->>AG: yesterday's state
    AG->>AG: diff → ACCESS_LOST · MODEL_ADDED<br/>MODEL_REMOVED · PRICE_CHANGED<br/>ENTITLEMENT_CHANGED
    alt something actually changed
        AG->>SNS: publish alert
    else nothing changed
        AG--)AG: stay silent
        note right of AG: a daily "all clear" email<br/>is a daily "ignore me" email
    end
    AG->>DB: write SNAPSHOT + EVENTs
    end

    rect rgba(201, 174, 255, 0.18)
    note over AG,DB: Phase 3 — behaviour contracts
    loop each live contract
        AG->>TGT: replay cases × 3 repetitions × every target
        TGT-->>AG: outputs
        AG->>AG: assert → aggregate → assign tier<br/>(in code, never by a model)
        AG->>DB: write RUN summary
    end
    end
